<title>NETHERLANDS: RESEARCH - Bangert cuts KLM EPS estimates.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH - Bangert cuts KLM EPS estimates.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1996-11-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Summary of Nov 12 research.</p>
<p>Company---------Sector--------Price---Broker----------------</p>
<p>    KLM		 airline	 42.30   Bangert Pontier</p>
<p>COMMENT: Sell (vs Hold). After the disappointing Q2 results we lowered our EPS estimates. We reduced our EPS estimate for 1996/97 from 5.85 guilders to 4.25 guilders and 1997/98 to 3.85 guilders from 6.00. We have lowered our EPS estimates, based on a strong increase in the break even load factor (lack of control of costs) which will be partly compensated by lower interest charges. KLM  will continue to destroy value in the next few years, which makes the stock a fundamental sell.</p>
<p>    Estimates (Dfl):   EPS	pvs	P/E     Dividend</p>
<p>    1995 (actual)	 5.86		  9.6     2.00</p>
<p>    1996		    4.25   (5.85)    10.0     1.50</p>
<p>    1997		    3.85   (6.00)    11.0     1.50</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom, +31 20 504 5000 (Fax +31 20 504 5040)</p>
